title: N-able N-central Authentication Bypass Exploitation
id: a92a7458-baa6-4c0e-891a-5f031c782489
status: experimental
description: Detects exploitation of N-able N-central authentication bypass chain (CVE-2026-86206 + CVE-2026-86207) where a semicolon/Forwarded header bypass tricks the Jetty application into treating a remote request as loopback, followed by 2FA bypass. An attacker can gain full admin access to N-central RMM platform via TCP 8443.
references:
  - https://www.n-able.com/blog/n-central-security-hotfix-september-5-2026
  - https://www.rapid7.com
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-09-10
tags:
  - attack.t1190
  - attack.t1078
logsource:
  category: network_connection
  product: linux
detection:
  selection_forwarded_header:
    dst_port: 8443
  filter_loopback:
    src_ip: '127.0.0.1'
  selection_admin_creation:
    dst_port: 8443
    http_request_uri|contains: '/api/user'
    http_request_method: 'POST'
  condition: selection_admin_creation or (selection_forwarded_header and not filter_loopback)
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate N-central admin console access
level: high
